To enhance the decision-making logic in the queue handler, we can implement a priority-based system that evaluates requests based on their urgency before processing.

Here's an updated version of `handler.js`:

```javascript
const Queue = require('bull');
const queue = new Queue('requestQueue');

queue.process(async (job) => {
    const { request } = job.data;
    // Decision logic based on request priority
    if (request.priority === 'high') {
        await processHighPriority(request);
    } else {
        await processLowPriority(request);
    }
});

async function processHighPriority(request) {
    // Implement high-priority processing logic
}

async function processLowPriority(request) {
    // Implement low-priority processing logic
}
```

Also, ensure to update your `settings.json` to allow configurable priority levels:

```json
{
  "priorityLevels": ["low", "normal", "high"]
}
```

After modifying the logic, run tests to ensure functionality:

```bash
npm run test
```

Make sure to add new test cases in `handler.test.js` that cover various priority scenarios.
